From 93edd0b20f87949fa79f8c9bda84783086d6de61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:04:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Resolve CI-flake producer delivery through durable
 self-work receipts

CI intake assumed create returned a task ID, but declared intake queues a
courier request and can append to an owner with another primary key. Freeze
producer-owned declaration, route, identity and complete manifest before
submission; consume only authoritative route-bound completed receipts.

Add versioned selfwork-producer capabilities/prepare/advance CLI for headless
state adapters. Keep unknown/rejected/timeout outcomes pending with the same
snapshot. Never use local creation after declared submission. Core CI opts in
by explicit repository identity; product and unopted callers retain legacy
behavior, including already-attempted legacy pages. Keep guard/config policy
unchanged. Document the reusable snapshot and qualified owner contract.

Proof: canonical consumer run 42 files/2393 passes, additional 3 files/109
passes. Final focused suite 56 passes; 22 receipt/routing mutations killed
(after adding the append-created consistency case). Real producer CLI and
receiver/registry integration proves create, append, replay after courier
cache loss, one owner and one append comment. Journal tests cover queue
acknowledgment, timeout, restart, midnight, manifest growth and foreign routing.
Full scripts/check passes all 21 checks. No live production submission made.
